{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 852 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "34dac2b0a7d2750635ce6682054ac3e20a51e38c928b8c5520ef745590bb0a69" :edb/db-before-t 851 :edb/db-after-t 852 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534164 50 #inst "2026-10-06T06:41:38.207Z" 13194139534164 true] [17592186063923 1100 "Find the derivative of $y = \\arctan (-7x)$." 13194139534164 false] [17592186063923 1100 "Find the derivative of $y = \\arctan (-7x).$" 13194139534164 true] [17592186063923 1145 "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arctan x) = \\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\arctan (-7x)) \\\\\n&= (1)/(1 + (-7x)^{2}) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(-7x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{1 + 49x^{2}} \\cdot (-7) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{7}{1 + 49x^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534164 false] [17592186063923 1145 "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arctan x) = \\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-7x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(-7x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+49{x}^{2}}\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{1+49{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534164 true] [17592186063924 1100 "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$, if $y = \\arccos (5-8x)$." 13194139534164 false] [17592186063924 1100 "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x},$ if $y = \\arccos (5-8x).$" 13194139534164 true] [17592186063924 1145 "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arccos x) = -\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccos (5 - 8x)) \\\\\n&= - (1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (5 - 8x)^{2}}) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(5 - 8x) \\\\\n&= - (1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (25 - 80x + 64x^{2})}) \\cdot (-8) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80x - 24 - 64x^{2}}} \\\\\n&= (8)/(\\sqrt{4(20x - 6 - 16x^{2})}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{2\\sqrt{20x - 6 - 16x^{2}}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{20x - 6 - 16x^{2}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534164 false] [17592186063924 1145 "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arccos x) = -\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-8x)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5-8x)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-8x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(25-80x+64{x}^{2})}}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80x-24-64{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4(20x-6-16{x}^{2})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2\\sqrt{20x-6-16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{20x-6-16{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534164 true] [17592186063925 1100 "If $y= x \\arccos x$, calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$." 13194139534164 false] [17592186063925 1100 "If $y= x \\arccos x,$ calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" 13194139534164 true] [17592186063925 1145 "Applying the product rule and using the formula for the derivative of $\\arccos x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(x\\arccos x) &= x \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccos x) + \\arccos x\\frac{d}{dx}(x) \\\\\n&= x \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}) + \\arccos x \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}} + \\arccos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534164 false] [17592186063925 1145 "Applying the product rule and using the formula for the derivative of $\\arccos x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534164 true] [17592186063926 1100 "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x) = 5\\arcsin(3x^2)$." 13194139534164 false] [17592186063926 1100 "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x) = 5\\arcsin(3x^2).$" 13194139534164 true] [17592186063926 1145 "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsin x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(5\\arcsin (3x^{2})) \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot (1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (3x^{2})^{2}}) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(3x^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1 - 9x^{4}}} \\cdot (6x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{30x}{\\sqrt{1 - 9x^{4}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534164 false] [17592186063926 1145 "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsin x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3{x}^{2})^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{4}}}\\cdot (6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{30x}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534164 true] [17592186064277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279817 13194139534164 true] [17592186064277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279824 13194139534164 true] [17592186064277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279834 13194139534164 true] [17592186064277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279837 13194139534164 true] [17592186064277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279840 13194139534164 true] [17592186064278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279775 13194139534164 true] [17592186064278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279782 13194139534164 true] [17592186064278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279831 13194139534164 true] [17592186064278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279844 13194139534164 true] [17592186064278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279851 13194139534164 true] [175921860